# Miss Loh Tutoring School — local scheduled jobs
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (add the line below)
#
# The server itself is kept running by a systemd service (miss-loh.service),
# not cron. The runner here is idempotent: each job records a SUCCESS row per
# window in the ScheduledRun table, so a job is only executed once per billing
# month / day. If the machine was off when a job was due, the first invocation
# after boot runs it automatically (recovery).

MAILTO=""
TZ=America/Toronto
*/30 * * * * /home/felix/projects/tutorschedule/scripts/run-jobs.sh >> /home/felix/projects/tutorschedule/logs/jobs.log 2>&1